.TH LUMEN-SYNC 1 "August 6, 2026" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
lumen-sync \- Sync the opencode lumen provider with the live NCSA Lumen catalog
.SH SYNOPSIS
lumen-sync [OPTIONS]
.SH DESCRIPTION
lumen-sync is a shell wrapper for lumen-sync.py that synchronizes the opencode \fBlumen\fP provider configuration with the live NCSA Lumen model catalog. It queries the Lumen API at \fBhttps://lumen.ncsa.illinois.edu/v1/models\fP and updates the \fIopencode.json\fP configuration file accordingly.

The tool adds real models from Lumen (with context/cost metadata), removes phantom entries not present in the Lumen catalog, and leaves other providers in the configuration untouched.

By default, lumen-sync performs a dry-run showing what changes would be made without modifying any files. Use the \fB--apply\fP flag to actually update the configuration.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB--apply\fP
Write changes to opencode.json. A timestamped backup is created automatically (opencode.json.lumen-sync-backup-YYYYMMDD-HHMMSS).
.TP
\fB--list\fP
Print the live Lumen catalog with model names, context windows, and pricing, then exit. No changes are made to opencode.json.
.TP
\fB--no-prune\fP
When used with \fB--apply\fP, adds/updates models from Lumen but preserves existing opencode.json entries that are not present in the Lumen catalog (disables pruning).
.TP
\fB--help\fP
Display help message and exit.
.TP
\fB--version\fP
Print version information and exit.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
\fBLUMEN_API_KEY\fP
Required. Must be set to your NCSA Lumen API key. The script reads this from the environment for API authentication and never writes it to configuration files.
Set it in your shell profile (e.g., ~/.bashrc, ~/.zshrc) for persistent access:
    export LUMEN_API_KEY=your_actual_key_here
.SH FILES
.TP
\fI~/lumen-sync.py\fP
The underlying Python script that performs the actual synchronization (stdlib only).
.TP
\fI~/lumen-sync\fP
This shell wrapper script (forwards all arguments to lumen-sync.py).
.TP
\fI~/.config/opencode/opencode.json\fP
The opencode configuration file that gets modified (when using \fB--apply\fP).
.TP
\fIopencode.json.lumen-sync-backup-*.\fP
Timestamped backups created automatically before applying changes.
.SH EXAMPLES
.PP
Preview what changes would be made (dry-run):
    lumen-sync
.PP
Apply changes to opencode.json (creates automatic backup):
    lumen-sync --apply
.PP
View the current Lumen model catalog:
    lumen-sync --list
.PP
Apply changes but keep existing config entries not in Lumen:
    lumen-sync --apply --no-prune
.PP
Set up persistent API key (add to your shell profile):
    echo 'export LUMEN_API_KEY=your_key_here' >> ~/.zshrc
    source ~/.zshrc
.SH EXIT STATUS
0   Success.
1   Error (e.g., missing API key, network issues, or file permissions).
2   Invalid command-line usage.
